oved, Paid, Written off), the invoice and how many versions were sent, what was billed, approved and paid, and the aging. Search by claim, booking, renter, insurer, adjuster or plate; the tiles open what is still to invoice and what is over 30 or 60 days. Finance and customer service have the same page in the staff portal.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="insurance-replacements-rates-and-billing-add-one-in-a-minute" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add one in a minute</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add an insurance replacement</b>. Only the renter&#39;s name, the insurer, the claim number and the dates are needed; the phone and the email are optional.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">To fill it from an email, paste the adjuster&#39;s email or the claim notice in <b class="gd-ui">Paste text</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Read it</b>. Check what was found, then press <b class="gd-ui">Use these</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The car: a car of the fleet, or <b class="gd-ui">Not in the fleet (type it)</b> with its year, make, model and plate. A car typed in never shows in the fleet, on the calendars or to an owner.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Off the calendar and owner notices</b> is always on for a car typed in, and a choice for a fleet car. It can be switched later on the rental (<b class="gd-ui">Take off the calendar</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Put on the calendar</b>).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add the rental</b>. The form saves as a draft while you type: an unfinished one waits in Unfinished rentals, and a discarded one comes back with <b class="gd-ui">Restore it</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" i