ass="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">To use the phone&#39;s own phone and messages apps instead, turn off <b class="gd-ui">Call and Text buttons go through Quo</b> in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>. With Phone and texts off, the buttons use the phone&#39;s own apps too.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-the-carmacars-app-links" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The CarmaCars app links</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, card The CarmaCars app (App Store and Google Play). Paste the App Store link (https://apps.apple.com/...) and the Google Play link (https://play.google.com/...) once the apps are live and press Save. From then on, iPhones and Android phones browsing the site see <b class="gd-ui">Download the CarmaCars app</b> in the footer and in the alerts invitation, with the link of their own store. Empty, nothing shows.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-who-is-calling-the-caller-pop-up-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Who is calling: the caller pop-up (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">When someone calls the CarmaCars number, a panel opens at the bottom right of every Admin page (across the bottom on a phone) while the phone rings, and stays while the call goes on and for 3 minutes after it ends. Customer service get the same panel in their portal. The number is matched to the renter on file (their mobile or their account holder&#39;s), the same way Texts and calls matches it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A renter: their name, the booking on rent (or the next one coming) with the car, the balance they owe now (rental payments due and unpaid charges after a rental, <b class="gd-ui">overdue</b> when a payment is late), the deposit (held, waived, released, or not taken yet), what they are waiting on (a booking request or offer, a change, a question to them, an open To do) and the last three notes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Write what the call was about in <b class="gd-ui">Note about this call</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Add note</b>: it is kept on the renter with the time, your name and the booking.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Open the renter&#39;s page</b> opens the full record. The booking opens from its line.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An unknown number shows <b class="gd-ui">Unknown caller</b>: press <b class="gd-ui">Create lead</b> to keep it as a phone lead, then open the conversation in Texts and calls to name it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press the cross to close a call; it stays closed in this browser. The panel checks for calls every 10 seconds while you use the portal (once a minute when the page is left alone).</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-calls-through-the-site-open-the-pop-up-too-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls through the site open the pop-up too (release 48)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A call you place from the site (the Call button, the phone in your browser) opens the pop-up at once with the Call helper, for you only. It says <b class="gd-ui">Your call: on now</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Call ended</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A call to the CarmaCars number that rings the browsers opens the pop-up for everyone it rings (customer service and Sales, as set in Program settings), and for every Admin. When someone answers, it says <b class="gd-ui">On the phone now</b> and the history names who took it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The pop-up opens within about a second of the ring: it no longer waits for the 10 second check. Every office role gets it: customer service, Fleet, Sales and Finance.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Every call through the site is recorded (both sides), turned into text and summarised. On the renter&#39;s page, choose <b class="gd-ui">Calls</b> in the Activity log: each call shows the date, in or out, who took it, how long, <b class="gd-ui">Play</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Show the transcript</b> and the summary. The booking&#39;s history shows the same.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Quo calls show Quo&#39;s recording, transcript and summary there too. When Quo sends no summary, the site writes a one line summary from the transcript.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Calls of the last 60 days that were missing a recording, transcript or summary are looked up once at Twilio and at Quo, a few every five minutes.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-minimize-the-pop-up-and-the-call-helper-release-43" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Minimize the pop-up, and the Call helper (release 43)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The line at the top right of a call minimizes it to a small chip at the bottom of the page: the caller&#39;s name and the call&#39;s timer. A click anywhere outside the panel, or Esc, minimizes it too; nothing is closed by accident. Press the chip to open the call again. The cross still closes a call in this browser, and a new call always opens by itself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Inside each call, the <b class="gd-ui">Call helper</b> is for new hires: <b class="gd-ui">Say</b> (the greeting, with the staff member&#39;s first name and the caller&#39;s name and booking when known), a button for each situation with 3 to 6 short steps and links to the right page of their portal, and <b class="gd-ui">Search the quick answers</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Hide</b> puts it away in that browser.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">You write all of it in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Call helper</b> (see Settings). <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> on the helper takes you there.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-renter-notes-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Renter notes (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every renter page has <b class="gd-ui">Add a note</b>, and its Activity log lists the notes (chip <b class="gd-ui">Notes</b>): what staff noted about the renter, newest first, with the date and time, who wrote it and their role, the booking and the words during a call when it was written from the pop-up. Admins and office staff add notes; nobody can change one. To take one away, press <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> and give the reason: it is no longer shown, and the note, the removal and the reason stay in the audit log. The same notes show on the caller pop-up, on a renter&#39;s conversation in Texts and calls, and on the staff portal&#39;s renter.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-the-call-button-through-twilio-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Call button through Twilio (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Since release 44 calls are made and taken in the browser (below); ringing the staff member&#39;s own cell first is a Program setting, off by default. The release 35 way: <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> on a staff page rings the staff member&#39;s own cell, then connects the customer with the CarmaCars number as caller ID, and logs the call with its length and outcome on the renter, lead or booking. It needs the GitHub secrets TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID, TWILIO_API_KEY and TWILIO_API_SECRET (and the CarmaCars number as a verified caller ID in Twilio); until then <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> opens Quo and says why. A staff member with no mobile on their profile is asked for it the first time they press <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> (a Canadian or US mobile, saved without a texted code), then the call starts (release 40).</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-calls-in-the-browser-release-44" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls in the browser (release 44)</h2><p class="gd-p">Staff, Admins included, make and take calls in the browser of the staff and Admin portals, with the CarmaCars number as caller ID. Staff abroad never use their own international number.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Call</b> anywhere opens the call screen (a card at the bottom left on a computer, the whole screen on a phone): the name and number, then the timer, <b class="gd-ui">Mute</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Keypad</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Speaker</b> (microphone and speaker choice), <b class="gd-ui">Hold</b> and the red <b class="gd-ui">End call</b>, which is always on the screen and also cancels a call that is still starting. Switching apps on a phone keeps the call on; closing the page ends a call that is still starting. The round green phone button at the bottom left opens <b class="gd-ui">Keypad</b> (any number) and <b class="gd-ui">Contacts</b> (the people called last, or a search of renters and leads; Sales see only their own leads, masked). The browser asks once for the microphone. The call is kept on the person&#39;s history with its length and its recording, as before.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A call to the business number rings the browsers of the staff who have a staff page open, by role (customer service and Sales by default), each with <b class="gd-ui">Answer</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b>. Sales sees the caller&#39;s name or the number hidden.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Nobody online or nobody answered: the caller hears the message of Program settings and it is a missed call with its task and its text back, like every missed call. With a forward number set, the call goes there instead. Never to a staff member&#39;s own number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, the phone settings: <b class="gd-ui">Calls in the browser</b> (on), Whose browser rings (cs, sales; add admin, fleet or finance), <b class="gd-ui">Ring for (seconds)</b> (25), <b class="gd-ui">Calls in the browser: nobody answered, forward to</b> (empty), <b class="gd-ui">Calls in the browser: nobody answered, the message</b>, and Ring my own mobile first (the release 35 way, off).</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Setting up Twilio once: save the GitHub repository secrets TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID (AC...), TWILIO_API_KEY (an API key SID, SK...), TWILIO_API_SECRET (that key&#39;s secret) and TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN (the account&#39;s Auth Token, which checks every request from Twilio), and TWILIO_CALLER_ID (the business number, for example +12895550123) when it differs from the CarmaCars number of Site settings. The business number must be a Twilio number or a verified caller ID in Twilio. The site makes the TwiML App &quot;CarmaCars browser calls&quot; itself, and points a Twilio business number with no Voice URL at the site. For incoming calls to ring browsers, calls to the business number must reach that Twilio number (buy it in Twilio, or forward to it). Until all is set, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> says what is missing.</div></aside><p class="gd-p">Sales sees customer numbers hidden. Viewing as a Sales rep, <b class="gd-ui">Reveal</b> shows a number; every reveal is in the audit log.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-unanswered" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Unanswered</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Leads</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Unanswered</b> (customer service has it too): every customer text with no reply and every missed call not called back, oldest first. <b class="gd-ui">Reply</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Call back</b> opens the conversation; <b class="gd-ui">Mark answered</b> when it was answered another way. A customer waiting more than 15 minutes (Program settings, <b class="gd-ui">Unanswered SLA minutes</b>) alerts customer service and the Admins once. WhatsApp is not in the list: the morning digest reminds you to check it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-call-recording-and-transcripts-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Call recording and transcripts (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Calls placed from the site&#39;s Call button are recorded from the moment the customer answers. No caller notice plays.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The recording is copied to CarmaCars&#39; private storage and deleted at Twilio once our copy is safe (Program settings, on by default).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">It is turned into text with the free daily AI allowance; when the allowance is used, the call waits for the next day.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The transcript, its summary and Play recording show on the renter&#39;s, the lead&#39;s, the booking&#39;s and the conversation&#39;s history, for Admins, customer service and Sales.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The transcript feeds the renter&#39;s and the lead&#39;s intent at once (hot, warm or cold, with what they said they want).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Recording and deleting at Twilio are two switches in Program settings, under the phone settings.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-calls-first-texts-after-release-37" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls first, texts after (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Call before you text.</b> On a lead, a renter or a booking, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> is the first button and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> the second.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On your To do and on <b class="gd-ui">Unanswered</b>, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'discount-games-and-leads', 'chapter', 'leads-and-sales-claims', 'Everyone gets one quick game, signed in or not: spin the wheel, scratch to reveal, quick blackjack, cup shuffle, Plinko, the card pack, coin flip, dice roll, slot machine, prize drop or mystery box. Every play wins a promo code or another go. To see the code they give a first name and an email (a mobile number is optional), so you get a lead. A signed-in renter has their name and email filled in from their account: one tap on **Get my code**, and the code is tied to their account (Rewards, Your discounts) and applies at checkout. It is on by default; nothing needs setting up.

## What the visitor sees

- On the 2nd page view (any page) or after 30 seconds on the site, whichever first, or (on a computer) when the mouse heads for the tabs. A card slides in at the bottom; on a phone it is a sheet at the bottom, never a full-screen block, and it always closes.
- Never inside a portal (account, admin, staff, owner, investor, field) or on booking, checkout, pay, sign or sign-in pages, never on the first page of a visit from a search engine on a phone, never over the cookie banner; no new game for someone already known by email or with a booking request in progress. Once a visit by default, and again on every new visit (a visit ends after 30 minutes away), also when they closed it without playing. Settings > Discount games has Preview the game, to see it any time, signed in or not. Staff and admin see and play the game on the site too, as a preview of what visitors see: their claim says "Staff can''t use game codes: this is a preview of what visitors see." and no code is made.
- After claiming a code: no game for the rest of that visit. A day after their latest claim the game comes back on their next visit with the usual timings, a new game and a new draw, and they can win another code. The day counts for the browser, the email, the mobile number and the account; within it the game says when they can play again. A visitor known only through their own claim still gets it; one known through a booking request or the chat, not signed in, does not.
- Won and not claimed: a small badge "Your 5% off is saved" with **Get my code** and **Play again** stays on the pages. On a later visit, at the moment a first game would show, the prize pops up by itself once as a small slide-in at the bottom ("Your 5% off is still waiting", the same two buttons), never as a card over the page; closed, it does not come back in that visit. Until they claim it or the prize ends after 14 days.
- **Play again** on a prize not claimed: a new, different game with a new draw. They keep the better of the two prizes and the other is closed, so there is only ever one code to claim: the card says "You won 15% off" or "You keep your 5% off". Once a visit and once a day (a setting).
- Every play wins: 5% off (54 in 100), 10% off (25), another go (15), 15% off (4), $50 off a rental of 3 days or more (1), 25% off up to $150 (0.6), $100 off a rental of 4 days or more (0.3) or one free day on a rental of 3 days or more (0.1). The prize is decided before the game starts; the game only shows it. The short terms with the game list the prizes and say the chances differ.
- Another go: the card says "You won another go!" and **Play again** starts a second, different game whose prize is drawn from the discounts only, so it always ends in a code. One replay at a time; it is never a code itself. Closed before pressing it, the card offers it again next time.
- The code (for example WIN-7KQ4-XM2P) comes off the rental charge only, up to $75 for a percentage, on one booking, within 7 days, one code a day per person, email, phone and device, never with another code. An earlier code not used yet stays good until it ends. The email with the code goes either way; a reminder goes 3 days before its last day and another the day before (Promo codes). Offers only with the marketing box ticked.
- On this device the code fills itself into the promo code box of the request form. Like every promo code, the discount is shared with the owner in the split.

## Leads

**People** > **Renters**, the **Leads** tab.

1. The tiles: plays, claims, codes on booking requests, bookings, revenue and discounts from game codes in the last 30 days, then the same by game and by prize (Play again shows its plays; it has no claims).
2. Each claim: when, the name (and "on the site now"), email and phone, the prize and game, the code and whether it is used (with the booking), marketing consent, and the visit: cars and pages viewed, minutes, city and device. A person who won again shows "2nd code of 2" under the name on each of their lines.
3. Press **Call** or **Email**, then **Contacted** (it is yours). **Close** with a reason when there is nothing more to do. A booking with the code marks the lead converted by itself.
4. A visitor who viewed 3 cars or more also gets a Sales task, for example "Claimed 10% off, viewed 6 cars: Maya". It closes when the code goes on a request. A new code while that task is open is added to it, not a second task.

## Contact details typed into forms

**People** > **Renters**, the **Leads** tab, the card "Typed into forms" at the top.

1. When someone types a name, email or phone into the request to book, the contact form, List your car, the owner application, Create an account, the discount game or the chat, it is saved as soon as each field is valid, even if they never press Send.
2. Each line: when, the name (and "On the site now"), email and phone, the form, and Sent or Not sent. "Email not confirmed" means the account was opened from the form and the person has not opened the link we emailed them yet.
3. After 30 minutes without sending, Sales'' queue gets "Unfinished request from Maya Chen: follow up" (not raised from 23:00 to 07:00, the quiet hours of the site alerts); To do shows it on the Sales line of Your teams. Call or email them; the task closes by itself when they send the form, or after 7 days (Program settings, Forms: close a Sales follow-up nobody answered after). The person stays on this list.
4. Only what they typed is saved, and never used for offers without their consent.

> Good to know: A new email gets an account at once (no password, email not confirmed) and one email "Continue your request" 30 minutes later, between 9:00 and 21:00. Until they open its link they cannot accept an offer, sign, pay or upload documents. An account never confirmed closes after 30 days; the lead stays. It is on by default; the times and the To do are in **Settings** > **Program**, the card "Forms left unfinished".

## Settings

**Settings** > **Discount games**.

- On or off, the cap for percentage codes ($75), how long a code is good for (7 days), when it shows (2nd page view, 30 seconds, exit intent), the days a visitor keeps their prize (14: closing never draws a new one, and a prize not claimed pops up again until then), the days after a claim before the game comes back (1; 0 is one code per person ever), how often Play again works on a prize not claimed (once a day; 0 turns it off), and the cars viewed for a Sales task (3). The reminders before a code ends are under Promo codes.
- At most one game a visit by default (a setting), and a visit ends after 30 minutes away (a setting): the next page brings the game again. With more than one a visit, the next card shows on their 3rd page view after a close (any page) or 2 minutes later, whichever first; no daily cap unless you set one. A prize waiting for them pops up once a visit only. All are settings. Never in the portals or on booking, checkout, payment or signing pages; the request-to-book form has its own game.
- Prizes and games: each prize with its percent, dollars or free days, a minimum rental length, its cap and its chance, or Play again (another go, at most one); each game''s weight (0 turns it off). Press **Save prizes and games**. Codes already sent keep their value.
